<p>
  After twenty years of building software — game programming at Ubisoft, ERP systems, logistics
  platforms serving millions of requests a day, and now enterprise AI — I decided it was time to
  have a place of my own on the web.
</p>

<p>This site has three jobs:</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    <strong>Show my work.</strong> My <a href="/career/">career</a> and
    <a href="/projects/">projects</a> pages tell the story better than any two-page resume can.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Share what I learn.</strong> I'm deeply invested in AI research and AI-assisted
    engineering. Articles here will cover agentic architectures, RAG in production, leading teams
    through the AI transition, and the mathematical foundations behind it all.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Start conversations.</strong> I'm always exploring ideas, and some of the best
    insights come from people thinking about the same problems. <a href="/contact/">Reach out</a>.
  </li>
</ol>

<p>
  The site itself is built with Astro and Tailwind CSS, deployed to GitHub Pages by GitHub
  Actions — simple, fast, and the whole thing is
  <a href="https://github.com/vasilegrafu/vasilegrafu.github.io">open source on my GitHub</a>.
</p>

<CalloutPart>
  More soon — including interactive articles with live charts, animations, and demos of the
